# Template for the EC2 host's /opt/macquiz/.env.production (docs/09-deployment.md
# section 8). scripts/aws/provision.sh copies this file there on first run;
# fill in real values and never commit the filled-in copy (.gitignore already
# excludes .env.production).
#
# docker-compose.prod.yml passes this whole file via env_file: to postgres,
# app, worker, backup, and alloy, so every var below must be set even though
# only some services read each one.

# --- Postgres ---
# MACQUIZ_DATABASE_URL below must embed the same user/password by hand -
# env_file values are not interpolated into each other.
POSTGRES_USER=macquiz
POSTGRES_PASSWORD=replace-with-a-generated-secret
POSTGRES_DB=macquiz

# --- App/worker (server/internal/config/config.go) ---
MACQUIZ_ADDR=:8080
MACQUIZ_ENV=production
MACQUIZ_DATABASE_URL=postgres://macquiz:replace-with-a-generated-secret@postgres:5432/macquiz?sslmode=disable
MACQUIZ_REDIS_URL=redis://redis:6379/0
# Signs JWT access tokens - generate a real random secret, do not reuse the
# dev-only default from config.go.
MACQUIZ_AUTH_SECRET=replace-with-a-generated-secret
# The origin the realtime /ws upgrade must accept from. The SPA and the API
# share one origin (see the Caddyfile header), so this is just DOMAIN.
MACQUIZ_WS_ALLOWED_ORIGINS=https://quiz.example.edu
MACQUIZ_IMPORT_DIR=/var/lib/macquiz/imports

# --- Object storage: bulk-import files and avatar photos ---
# One S3 bucket serves both (avatars live under an "avatars/" key prefix).
# Leave MACQUIZ_BLOB_BUCKET blank to keep using MACQUIZ_IMPORT_DIR and a
# local avatar directory instead - a shared Docker volume, fine on a single
# host below a few hundred concurrent imports, and the state this stack
# starts in before the buckets exist.
#
# Credentials are deliberately absent: on EC2 the instance role
# (scripts/aws/iam-policy.json) supplies them through IMDS, so no long-lived
# key pair sits in this file. Set MACQUIZ_BLOB_ACCESS_KEY_ID /
# MACQUIZ_BLOB_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY only when running outside AWS, and
# MACQUIZ_BLOB_ENDPOINT only for an S3-compatible service (R2, MinIO).
MACQUIZ_BLOB_BUCKET=macquiz-blobs
MACQUIZ_BLOB_REGION=ap-south-1
# MACQUIZ_BLOB_ENDPOINT=
# MACQUIZ_BLOB_ACCESS_KEY_ID=
# MACQUIZ_BLOB_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=

# --- Telemetry ---
# Grafana Cloud OTLP/HTTP metrics gateway (docs/10-operations.md section 2).
# Leave both blank to disable telemetry entirely (every instrument becomes a
# no-op) - safe for a first deploy before a Grafana Cloud account exists.
MACQUIZ_OTEL_EXPORTER_ENDPOINT=otlp-gateway-prod-xx-xxx-0.grafana.net/otlp
MACQUIZ_OTEL_EXPORTER_HEADERS=Authorization=Basic replace-with-base64-instanceid:token
# The `alloy` container (docs/10-operations.md section 3's "disk usage on the
# pg volume" threshold; scripts/grafana/alloy-disk-metrics.alloy) forwards to
# the same gateway above. It needs the Authorization header's value on its
# own (Alloy's config sets header name/value as separate fields, unlike the
# combined "name=value" string MACQUIZ_OTEL_EXPORTER_HEADERS uses) - same
# credential as MACQUIZ_OTEL_EXPORTER_HEADERS, just the part after
# "Authorization=".
MACQUIZ_ALLOY_OTLP_AUTH_HEADER=Basic replace-with-base64-instanceid:token

# --- Email ---
# Brevo API key (xkeysib-...) for the email leg of assignment-change notifications.
# Leave blank to disable email delivery entirely - the in-app
# user:{id}:notify channel still delivers the same quiz.assigned /
# quiz.unassigned event either way. (Amazon SES is the AWS-native
# alternative, but a new SES account is sandboxed until you request
# production access, which is a support ticket and a wait - not something
# to discover on launch day.)
MACQUIZ_EMAIL_API_KEY=replace-with-a-brevo-api-key
MACQUIZ_EMAIL_FROM=notify@example.edu
MACQUIZ_EMAIL_FROM_NAME=MacQuiz

# Public origin used only for the sign-in link in credential emails.
MACQUIZ_PUBLIC_URL=https://macquiz.svighnesh.tech

# Only read once, by the manual `docker compose run --rm app bootstrap`
# step (docker-compose.prod.yml's header comment) - not used by serve/worker.
MACQUIZ_BOOTSTRAP_ADMIN_EMAIL=admin@example.edu
MACQUIZ_BOOTSTRAP_ADMIN_PASSWORD=replace-with-a-generated-secret
MACQUIZ_BOOTSTRAP_ADMIN_NAME=Administrator

# --- Image + Caddy (docker-compose.prod.yml, Caddyfile) ---
# The image is built for the host's architecture by .github/workflows/deploy.yml
# (linux/arm64 for a t4g/Graviton instance).
MACQUIZ_IMAGE=ghcr.io/your-github-org/macquiz-app
TAG=latest
DOMAIN=quiz.example.edu

# --- Nightly backup (docs/10-operations.md section 1; scripts/backup) ---
# A second S3 bucket, dedicated to backups and separate from the blob bucket
# so a bug in the app's own storage path can never touch the dumps. Turn on
# bucket versioning (a console/CLI setting, done once at provisioning time,
# not by this repo) as the belt against a bad prune.
#
# Credentials again come from the instance role. AWS_REGION is what the AWS
# CLI inside the backup container reads; set BACKUP_S3_ENDPOINT only for an
# S3-compatible service.
BACKUP_S3_BUCKET=macquiz-backups
AWS_REGION=ap-south-1
# BACKUP_S3_ENDPOINT=
# Retention: 7 daily + 8 weekly dumps, pruned by the same nightly job.
BACKUP_DAILY_KEEP=7
BACKUP_WEEKLY_KEEP=8
# Optional dead-man's-switch (docs/10-operations.md section 3's "Backup job:
# nightly dump missing or failed" threshold): a Healthchecks.io (or
# compatible) check URL. backup.sh pings <url>/start on run, <url> on
# success, <url>/fail on failure; leave unset to skip. Not required.
# BACKUP_HEALTHCHECK_URL=https://hc-ping.com/replace-with-your-check-uuid
